msgid "Where available, record the date and time that the source was first created, which is a common and precise attribute on web and social media content. A creation timestamp may not be available for a source - if this is the case, leave this field blank and look for a publication or upload timestamp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:231
msgid "Where the time zone is indicated, convert the timestamp to UTC before entering it in this attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:234
msgid "source:uploaded_timestamp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:239
msgid "Date and time that the source was uploaded to the online platform or service on which it is hosted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:254
msgid "``:source/uploaded-at``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:259
#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:297
msgid "``2019-11-29T10:25:45Z``, ``2019``, ``2010-11-29``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:264
msgid "Where available, record the date and time that the source was uploaded to the online platform or service on which it is hosted. This may different from the date of creation or publication. Upload timestamp information may not be available for source - if this is the case, leave the field blank."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:266
msgid "If a publication date is not available for a source, the timestamp of the snapshot of the source found in the Internet Archive should be used in this field (and the :ref:`source:published_timestamp` would be left blank)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:268
#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:306
msgid "Where the time zone is indicated, convert the timestamp to UTC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:271
msgid "source:published_timestamp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:277
msgid "Date and time that the source was published."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:292
msgid "``:source/published-at``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:302
msgid "Where available, record the date and time that the source was published. This may different from the date of creation or upload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/source-source-specific.rst:304
msgid "Although a timestamp for creation and upload dates and times may not be available, it is very likely that at least a publication date will be available for a source. If a publication date is not available for a source, the timestamp of the snapshot of the source found in the Internet Archive should be used in the :ref:`source:uploaded_timestamp` and this field should be left blank."
msgstr ""

